</a>; cf. the phrases <span dir=\"rtl\">עשׂה הרע(ה) בעיני י׳ להכעיס(ו)</span> <em>do the evil in the eyes of Yahweh to provoke</em> (him) <em>to anger</em> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:25\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.25\">Dt 4:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 9:18\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.9.18\">9:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 31:29\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.31.29\">31:29</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:7\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.7\">1 K 16:7</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.17\">2 K 17:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 21:6\" href=\"/II_Kings.21.6\">21:6</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 33:6\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.33.6\">2 Ch 33:6</a>; so <span dir=\"rtl\">מכעסים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 21:15\" href=\"/II_Kings.21.15\">2 K 21:15</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:30\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.30\">Je 32:30</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כעס(ים) אשׁר הכעיס</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:30\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.30\">1 K 15:30</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.22\">21:22</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:26\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.26\">2 K 23:26</a>.—The phrase is characteristic of D Je and the compiler of Kings; see Dr<sup>Intr. 191;</sup> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:25\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.25\">Dt 4:25</a> Holz<sup>Einl. Hex. 287</sup>."}],"num":"2."}],"form":"Hiph."}]},"rid":"BDB04626","strong_numbers":["3707"],"next_hw":"כַּ֫עַס","prev_hw":"כֶּסֶת","all_cited":true,"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["4087"],"TWOT":["1016"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}